    add();add('The training budget was fixed before any new bank draw or fit: four independent uniform 128-board N12 subsets from each family, seeds 2026113200–2026113207. The source populations contain 472 zebra and 1,304 leaper boards, so the common label budget uses 27.118644% and 9.815951% of the respective populations. Within-family overlaps are retained and published. The eight source banks and optimizer trajectories are new; no bank is replaced after observing its graph or capacity.');add();add('Each conditional acquisition distribution draws 32 distinct raw positives uniformly from that fit’s N12 complement, excluding its 128 training boards. The remaining populations have 344 and 1,176 boards. A realized fit plus repair uses 160 raw labels. Raw and D4 arms share each acquisition draw; D4 attempts 256 correlated rotations/reflections before whole-board deduplication. The D4-invariance prior is supplied explicitly. This experiment uses additional same-size N12 positives and transfers to N13, unlike H3am’s intermediate N13 acquisition followed by N15 evaluation.');add();add('Every fit uses the unchanged H3ad grouped BP AdamW recipe: zero initialization, 4,000 updates, learning rate 0.3, cosine denominator 4,000, decay 0.01, betas (0.9,0.999), epsilon 1e−8, float32, TF32 disabled and no preconditioner. The exact pseudolikelihood aggregates all 298 one/two/three-clue subsets per source board, using occupied/free multiplicities 231/298. Counts, marginal exposures, inferred primitive lines and coefficient grouping are rebuilt independently for each bank. Before fitting, literal expanded-clue and actual-bank CPU/GPU loss/gradient checks pass. All eight fitted native source margins and retained weights are positive.');add();add('The positive-F derivative retains source-zero finite offsets with exposure at least ln(264/0.01), union the inferred lines. It keeps the fitted positive coefficients on F, zeroes unary/off-support entries, extends inferred lines and assigns newly representable off-line offsets zero. This supplied derivative is distinct from the native soft fitted energy. Support selection is based on source counts, exposure and the line prior; this study does not identify an optimizer advantage over an identically constructed count support.');add();add('The repair algorithm remains source-only: only inherited finite classes witnessed in selected positives or their D4 views may be deleted. All eight complements contain **zero observable inherited repair classes**, so every possible raw or D4 draw leaves its fitted support unchanged. The eight fitted models remain distinct parameter records, while their complete supports reduce to two graphs, one per family. Every positive-mass paired outcome is retained. There is one reachable paired union per fit and no favorable-outcome selection.');add();add('The evaluator computes exact without-replacement masses with a grouped binomial union dynamic program. It checks normalization at every dose 0–32; large integers are stored as decimal strings. The frozen complexity caps are 16 observable classes per fit, 512 reachable paired unions per dose per fit, and 256 full supports per family. Any cap failure would stop the entire study, with no pruning or extension. The independent audit cross-checks exact masses using a different closure/contained-union poset inversion. Here the single union has all choose(344,32) or choose(1176,32) mass.');add()
    add('| Family | Complete true N13 states | Complete 1/2/3-clue keys | Valid zero-F states | Invalid zero-F states | Exact graph fits |');add('|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|')
